            // requires the phi nodes at the TOP of a block, and emitStr below emits an
            // instruction of its own into this one.
            var youtV = bodyB.NewPhi([llvm.ir.NewIncoming(yidxElemV, yelemB),
                                      llvm.ir.NewIncoming(ystepElemV, joinB)])
            // The resume value is stored RAW - the shape test at headB is what reads it,
            // so a throw-in is forwarded rather than raised here.
            //
            // The yield itself sits inside a js_try, and the two arms answer the two
            // ways the driver can interrupt a parked yield*. The FINALLY closes the
            // delegate, which is what makes g.return() at a yield* run the delegate's
            // finally clauses (docs/todo.md 1.10): g.return() is gen_close, and
            // gen_close throws the GEN_EXIT sentinel AT this yield, so every js_try
            // between the yield and the body's entry runs its finally on the way out
            // and a barrier here is the one place the delegate handle is still
            // reachable. GEN_EXIT reaches the finally and NOT the catch, in either
            // engine (runtime.c's js_try, abnf/jsrt.go's genExit) - a close is a return
            // completion. The CATCH is g.throw(v), which raises an ordinary value at
